      "guidance": "Begin by navigating to an available open surface (countertop or shelf). Inspect it for the target object. If not found, proceed to another open surface. Only after exhausting visible open surfaces should you navigate to and inspect closed storage units like the fridge.",
      "hypothesis": "For perishable food items in mixed-layout kitchens, prioritizing inspection of open surfaces (countertops/shelves) before closed high-probability containers (fridge) yields fewer total search steps than starting with the semantically most likely container.",
